From 4c5a882b19051027d26faa7be010e46c0557aff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:25:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(geometry): read the base URL once per DOM state, and
 hit-test natively

Every getBoundingClientRect ran querySelector("base[href]") over the whole
document to check the prepared layout was reusable: 0.65 ms a read, 13 s
for one page snapshot on a Wikipedia article. Geometry reads now use the
memoized base URL, which DOM mutations invalidate.

document.elementFromPoint walked every element in JS, reading each rect
and the computed style of every ancestor: seconds a call on large pages,
and Input.dispatchMouseEvent calls it twice per click. The same hit test
(latest box in tree order that contains the point, is not
visibility-hidden, and is not clipped by an ancestor's overflow) now runs
over the prepared layout.
